// Title: RDP Port Forwarding Rule Added Via Netsh.EXE
// Sigma ID: 782d6f3e-4c5d-4b8c-92a3-1d05fed72e63
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), oscd.community
// Date: 2019-01-29 | Modified: 2023-02-13
// ATT&CK: lateral-movement, command-and-control, T1090
// Description: Detects the execution of netsh to configure a port forwarding of port 3389 (RDP) rule
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activity
// References:
//   - https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/01/bypassing-network-restrictions-through-rdp-tunneling.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_netsh_port_forwarding_3389.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\netsh.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "netsh.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " i" and ProcessCommandLine contains " p" and ProcessCommandLine contains "=3389" and ProcessCommandLine contains " c")
